  "cover_text": "Georgetown — Sally Long, a long-time resident of the Georgetown area, and fellow governors, will soon be joining the National League of Cities as their national program to provide support for individuals unable to vote in the month of November.\nThe National League of Cities, through its Board of Governors and the United Way of Greater Central Washington, announced the approval of the Orleansville Chapter of the openings and events board. The board will select the candidates from the March 27th Open Call for Governance and select Houston from the November 8th Open Calls, which is due by November 15.\nThe nominations and acknowledgments from the national geography must be submitted by March 27th of",
